ca.append(M(A,16,'Resonance width','C.1','The solid and dashed curves show the steady-state displacement amplitude of the same driven oscillator under two damping conditions. The driving-force amplitude is unchanged. Which conclusion is supported?', ['The dashed response has greater damping and a broader, lower resonance peak.','The dashed response has less damping and a broader, lower resonance peak.','The solid response has greater damping because its peak is taller.','The natural frequency must double when damping is increased.'],'Increased damping dissipates more energy per cycle and reduces the build-up of amplitude near resonance. Its response is lower and broader. A taller peak is a sign of less damping, and the data do not imply a doubled natural frequency.','6.pdf',8,'16','Damping and resonance response',plot(low,(0,2),(0,7),'driving frequency / natural frequency','amplitude / arbitrary units',(0,.5,1,1.5,2),(0,2,4,6),curve2=high)))
