ca.append(M(A,17,'Comparing orbital systems','D.1','A planet follows a circular orbit of radius $r$ and period $T$ about star X. Another planet orbits star Y with radius $2r$ and period $T/2$. Planet masses are negligible. What is $M_Y/M_X$?', ['$32$','$8$','$2$','$1/2$'],'From $T^2=4\\pi^2r^3/(GM)$, stellar mass is proportional to $r^3/T^2$. The ratio is $2^3/(1/2)^2=32$. The two planets orbit different stars, so one cannot use a constant $T^2/r^3$ for both without accounting for mass.','6.pdf',8,'17','Kepler scaling with central mass'))
