cb.append(M(B,13,'Refraction of sound','C.3','Sound travels from air into water at an incidence angle of $10^\\circ$ to the normal. The speeds are $340\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ and $1480\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$. What is the approximate refraction angle, and what happens to frequency?', ['$49^\\circ$; unchanged','$2.3^\\circ$; unchanged','$49^\\circ$; increased by a factor $4.35$','$10^\\circ$; unchanged'],'For waves $\\sin\\theta_1/\\sin\\theta_2=v_1/v_2$, giving $\\sin\\theta_2=(1480/340)\\sin10^\\circ=0.756$. Thus $\\theta_2\\approx49^\\circ$. Boundary oscillations preserve frequency; the wavelength increases.','a.pdf',6,'13','Refraction, wavelength and frequency'))
