cb.append(M(B,14,'Changing the second optical medium','C.3','A transparent solid has a critical angle of $30^\\circ$ at a solid-air boundary. The solid is immersed in liquid of refractive index $1.33$. What is the new critical angle at the solid-liquid boundary?', ['$42^\\circ$','$22^\\circ$','$30^\\circ$','$62^\\circ$'],"With air index $1$, $n_s=1/\\sin30^\\circ=2.00$. At the new boundary, $\\sin c=n_l/n_s=1.33/2=0.665$, so $c=41.7^\\circ$. The solid's refractive index has not changed; the index ratio has.",'a.pdf',7,'14','Critical angle and refractive-index ratios'))
cb.append(M(B,15,'Changing a vibrating string','C.4','A uniform string fixed at both ends has fundamental frequency $50\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$. Its vibrating length is increased by a factor $1.5$ and its tension by a factor $2.25$, without changing mass per unit length. What is its new third-harmonic frequency?', ['$150\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$','$100\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$','$225\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$','$337.5\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$'],'Wave speed is proportional to $\\sqrt F$, so it increases by $1.5$. Fundamental frequency is $v/(2L)$, and the same factor in length cancels this change. It remains $50\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$; the third harmonic is $150\\,\\mathrm{Hz}$.','a.pdf',7,'15','Standing-wave modes and changed conditions',svg(line(80,140,520,140,True)+circle(80,140,5)+circle(520,140,5)+'<path d="M80 140 Q153 30 227 140 Q300 250 373 140 Q447 30 520 140" fill="none" stroke="#202020" stroke-width="2"/>'+text(300,270,'third harmonic: three loops',15,'middle'),600,300)))
B.check('B16 recession-speed ratio',(.75/500)/(.65/650),1.5)
cb.append(M(B,16,'Comparing spectral redshifts','C.5','A spectral line of rest wavelength $500.00\\,\\mathrm{nm}$ is observed at $500.75\\,\\mathrm{nm}$ in star X. A line of rest wavelength $650.00\\,\\mathrm{nm}$ is observed at $650.65\\,\\mathrm{nm}$ in star Y. Both speeds are much less than $c$. What is $v_X/v_Y$?', ['$1.50$','$1.15$','$0.667$','$1.95$'],'For low speeds, $v/c=\\Delta\\lambda/\\lambda_0$. The ratio is $(0.75/500)/(0.65/650)=1.50$. Comparing shifts alone omits the different rest wavelengths. Both shifts are positive, so both sources recede.','a.pdf',7,'16','Small astronomical Doppler shifts'))
